{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000113",
  "title": "Heat Equation",
  "created_at": "2026-03-16T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-03-16T00:00:00Z",
  "shared_cargo_toml": null,
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_0",
      "source": "# \ud83d\udd25 2D Heat Equation\n\nThis notebook simulates the **2D heat equation** on an 800\u00d7800 grid using\nexplicit finite differences.\n\n## The Equation\n\n$$\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial t} = \\alpha \\nabla^2 u = \\alpha \\left( \\frac{\\partial^2 u}{\\partial x^2} + \\frac{\\partial^2 u}{\\partial y^2} \\right)$$\n\nwhere $u(x, y, t)$ is the temperature field and $\\alpha$ is the thermal\ndiffusivity. The discrete update (explicit Euler, 5-point stencil) is:\n\n$$u_{i,j}^{n+1} = u_{i,j}^{n} + \\alpha \\, \\Delta t \\left( u_{i+1,j}^{n} + u_{i-1,j}^{n} + u_{i,j+1}^{n} + u_{i,j-1}^{n} - 4\\, u_{i,j}^{n} \\right)$$\n\nStability requires $4 \\alpha \\, \\Delta t < 1$ (CFL condition for 2D diffusion).\n\n### Initial Conditions\n\n- **Hot spots** \u2014 several circular regions start at high temperature (white/yellow).\n- **Cool spots** \u2014 circular regions start at zero (dark blue).\n- **Warm bottom edge** \u2014 the entire bottom row is held at constant high temperature, continuously feeding heat upward.\n- **Orbiting source** \u2014 a roving hot spot orbits the centre of the grid, gently leaking heat into the cells it passes over.\n\n### Boundary Conditions\n\n| Edge | Condition |\n|------|-----------|\n| Top | Cold ($u = 0$) \u2014 heat sink |\n| Left | Cold ($u = 0$) \u2014 heat sink |\n| Right | Cold ($u = 0$) \u2014 heat sink |\n| Bottom | Warm ($u = 1$) \u2014 constant source |\n\nThe diffusion coefficient $\\alpha = 0.25$ with 10 sub-steps per frame keeps\nthe simulation stable while evolving quickly enough to watch.",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Description",
      "cell_type": "Markdown"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_1",
      "source": "/// # 2D Heat Equation Simulation\n///\n/// Solves the 2D heat equation  **\u2202u/\u2202t = \u03b1 \u2207\u00b2u**  on a 800\u00d7800 grid\n/// using explicit finite differences.  Several hot and cold spots seed\n/// the initial temperature field.  The bottom edge is held at a constant\n/// high temperature, and a roving hot spot orbits the center \u2014 it doesn't\n/// overwrite cells, but gently leaks heat into them from behind.  Watch\n/// the interplay as heat diffuses through the cool spots.\n\nconst W: u32 = 800;\nconst H: u32 = 800;\nconst N: usize = W as usize;\nconst M: usize = H as usize;\nconst ALPHA: f64 = 0.25;\n\n// Orbiting heat source parameters.\nconst ORBIT_RADIUS: f64 = 200.0;\nconst ORBIT_SPEED: f64 = 0.03;\nconst SPOT_RADIUS: usize = 30;\nconst SPOT_LEAK: f64 = 0.03;\n\nstruct HeatEquation {\n    u: Vec<f64>,\n    buf: Vec<f64>,\n    step: u32,\n}\n\nimpl HeatEquation {\n    fn idx(x: usize, y: usize) -> usize {\n        y * N + x\n    }\n\n    fn temp_to_color(t: f64) -> (u8, u8, u8) {\n        // Cool (dark blue) \u2192 warm (orange/yellow) \u2192 hot (white).\n        let t = t.clamp(0.0, 1.0);\n        if t < 0.25 {\n            let s = t / 0.25;\n            let r = (10.0 + s * 20.0) as u8;\n            let g = (10.0 + s * 10.0) as u8;\n            let b = (40.0 + s * 160.0) as u8;\n            (r, g, b)\n        } else if t < 0.5 {\n            let s = (t - 0.25) / 0.25;\n            let r = (30.0 + s * 200.0) as u8;\n            let g = (20.0 + s * 60.0) as u8;\n            let b = (200.0 - s * 100.0) as u8;\n            (r, g, b)\n        } else if t < 0.75 {\n            let s = (t - 0.5) / 0.25;\n            let r = (230.0 + s * 25.0) as u8;\n            let g = (80.0 + s * 140.0) as u8;\n            let b = (100.0 - s * 80.0) as u8;\n            (r, g, b)\n        } else {\n            let s = (t - 0.75) / 0.25;\n            let r = 255;\n            let g = (220.0 + s * 35.0) as u8;\n            let b = (20.0 + s * 235.0) as u8;\n            (r, g, b)\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Gently leak heat into a circular region \u2014 adds `amount` to each cell\n    /// without exceeding 1.0, simulating a source behind the grid.\n    fn leak_circle(u: &mut [f64], cx: usize, cy: usize, r: usize, amount: f64) {\n        let r2 = (r * r) as f64;\n        let x_min = cx.saturating_sub(r);\n        let x_max = (cx + r).min(N - 1);\n        let y_min = cy.saturating_sub(r);\n        let y_max = (cy + r).min(M - 1);\n        for y in y_min..=y_max {\n            for x in x_min..=x_max {\n                let dx = x as f64 - cx as f64;\n                let dy = y as f64 - cy as f64;\n                if dx * dx + dy * dy <= r2 {\n                    let i = Self::idx(x, y);\n                    u[i] = (u[i] + amount).min(1.0);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn set_circle(u: &mut [f64], cx: usize, cy: usize, r: usize, temp: f64) {\n        let r2 = (r * r) as f64;\n        let x_min = cx.saturating_sub(r);\n        let x_max = (cx + r).min(N - 1);\n        let y_min = cy.saturating_sub(r);\n        let y_max = (cy + r).min(M - 1);\n        for y in y_min..=y_max {\n            for x in x_min..=x_max {\n                let dx = x as f64 - cx as f64;\n                let dy = y as f64 - cy as f64;\n                if dx * dx + dy * dy <= r2 {\n                    u[Self::idx(x, y)] = temp;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Simulation for HeatEquation {\n    fn init() -> Self {\n        let mut u = vec![0.0; N * M];\n\n        // Hot spots.\n        Self::set_circle(&mut u, N / 4, M / 4, 40, 1.0);\n        Self::set_circle(&mut u, 3 * N / 4, M / 4, 30, 0.9);\n        Self::set_circle(&mut u, N / 2, 3 * M / 4, 50, 1.0);\n\n        // Cool spots.\n        Self::set_circle(&mut u, 3 * N / 4, 3 * M / 4, 36, 0.0);\n        Self::set_circle(&mut u, N / 4, 3 * M / 4, 24, 0.0);\n\n        // Warm bottom edge (constant heat source).\n        for x in 0..N {\n            u[Self::idx(x, M - 1)] = 1.0;\n        }\n\n        let buf = u.clone();\n        Self { u, buf, step: 0 }\n    }\n\n    fn tick(&mut self) -> Canvas {\n        // Run several diffusion sub-steps per frame for visible evolution.\n        for _ in 0..10 {\n            for y in 1..M - 1 {\n                for x in 1..N - 1 {\n                    let c = Self::idx(x, y);\n                    let laplacian = self.u[Self::idx(x + 1, y)]\n                        + self.u[Self::idx(x - 1, y)]\n                        + self.u[Self::idx(x, y + 1)]\n                        + self.u[Self::idx(x, y - 1)]\n                        - 4.0 * self.u[c];\n                    self.buf[c] = self.u[c] + ALPHA * laplacian;\n                }\n            }\n            std::mem::swap(&mut self.u, &mut self.buf);\n\n            // Re-apply warm bottom edge.\n            for x in 0..N {\n                self.u[Self::idx(x, M - 1)] = 1.0;\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Orbiting hot spot: leak heat in a circle that drifts around the center.\n        let angle = self.step as f64 * ORBIT_SPEED;\n        let cx = (N as f64 / 2.0 + ORBIT_RADIUS * angle.cos()) as usize;\n        let cy = (M as f64 / 2.0 + ORBIT_RADIUS * angle.sin()) as usize;\n        Self::leak_circle(&mut self.u, cx, cy, SPOT_RADIUS, SPOT_LEAK);\n\n        self.step += 1;\n\n        Canvas::from_fn(W, H, |x, y| {\n            let t = self.u[Self::idx(x as usize, y as usize)];\n            Self::temp_to_color(t)\n        })\n    }\n\n    fn fps() -> u32 {\n        30\n    }\n}",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "order": 1,
      "label": "Heat Diffusion",
      "cell_type": "Code",
      "collapsed": true
    }
  ],
  "description": "Watch heat diffuse across a 2D surface in real time using the Simulation trait.",
